# Simple answers only (HARD)

Andrew runs 20+ projects. Every reply must be easy to scan in 10 seconds.

## Default shape

1. **Link first** (if there is one)
2. **Verdict** — 3–5 bullets max: match / different / on purpose
3. **What to do** — one line (approve, pick A/B, or nothing)

## Forbidden unless he says "explain"

- Token tables, clamp math, "banner vs display" jargon
- Multi-section essays, process narration, "here's what I found"
- Making him re-instruct the same format turn after turn

## Type / font questions

- Give a **compare mock** (`docs/*.html`) + **plain English** under each sample: font · weight · style · size
- Say **MATCH** or **DIFFERENT** — not "Type OS Display tier"
- Buy-box lede = separate row; never mix into body/50/50 compare unless asked

## Mock deliverables

When comparing fonts or layouts: one HTML file, side-by-side, verdict at top, link when pushed to GitHub Pages.
